{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "cues": [
    {
      "id": "vermeer-forgery-cue-1",
      "transcript": "To defend himself, this painter had to prove his masterpiece was a fake.",
      "file": "audio/vermeer-forgery/narration/cue-1.wav",
      "start": 0,
      "duration": 4.675,
      "beatIndex": 0,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "vermeer-forgery.asset.forgery-defense.script.1",
      "samples": 112200,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "vermeer-forgery-cue-2",
      "transcript": "In 1945, Han van Meegeren was arrested on suspicion of collaboration. A supposed Vermeer had reached Hermann Göring, a leading Nazi, through an art dealer.",
      "file": "audio/vermeer-forgery/narration/cue-2.wav",
      "start": 4.933333333333334,
      "duration": 11.325,
      "beatIndex": 1,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "vermeer-forgery.asset.forgery-defense.script.2",
      "samples": 271800,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "vermeer-forgery-cue-3",
      "transcript": "His defense was that he had painted it himself. But some experts resisted believing that their celebrated Vermeers were forgeries.",
      "file": "audio/vermeer-forgery/narration/cue-3.wav",
      "start": 16.4,
      "duration": 8.375,
      "beatIndex": 2,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "vermeer-forgery.asset.forgery-defense.script.3",
      "samples": 201000,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "vermeer-forgery-cue-4",
      "transcript": "He had exploited a gap in Vermeer’s known early work. Religious paintings filled what experts expected to find. A prominent scholar endorsed one; a museum bought it.",
      "file": "audio/vermeer-forgery/narration/cue-4.wav",
      "start": 25.033333333333335,
      "duration": 11.35,
      "beatIndex": 3,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "vermeer-forgery.asset.forgery-defense.script.4",
      "samples": 272400,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "vermeer-forgery-cue-5",
      "transcript": "He used old canvases, then heated modern resin-based paint until it hardened. Cracking that surface made new paint look centuries old.",
      "file": "audio/vermeer-forgery/narration/cue-5.wav",
      "start": 36.53333333333333,
      "duration": 9.175,
      "beatIndex": 4,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "vermeer-forgery.asset.forgery-defense.script.5",
      "samples": 220200,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "vermeer-forgery-cue-6",
      "transcript": "But court-appointed examiners tested the materials. They found evidence of modern synthetic resin, matching materials from his studio.",
      "file": "audio/vermeer-forgery/narration/cue-6.wav",
      "start": 45.86666666666667,
      "duration": 8.775,
      "beatIndex": 5,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "vermeer-forgery.asset.forgery-defense.script.6",
      "samples": 210600,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "vermeer-forgery-cue-7",
      "transcript": "X-rays revealed another problem: separate crack patterns in the old layers underneath and the newer painting above.",
      "file": "audio/vermeer-forgery/narration/cue-7.wav",
      "start": 54.8,
      "duration": 7.425,
      "beatIndex": 6,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "vermeer-forgery.asset.forgery-defense.script.7",
      "samples": 178200,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "vermeer-forgery-cue-8",
      "transcript": "The evidence supported his confession. An old canvas did not make the painting an old master.",
      "file": "audio/vermeer-forgery/narration/cue-8.wav",
      "start": 62.36666666666667,
      "duration": 6.2,
      "beatIndex": 7,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "vermeer-forgery.asset.forgery-defense.script.8",
      "samples": 148800,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "vermeer-forgery-cue-9",
      "transcript": "The collaboration case fell away. The fraud did not. In 1947, he was convicted of fraud and forgery, and sentenced to one year.",
      "file": "audio/vermeer-forgery/narration/cue-9.wav",
      "start": 68.8,
      "duration": 9.6,
      "beatIndex": 8,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "vermeer-forgery.asset.forgery-defense.script.9",
      "samples": 230400,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "vermeer-forgery-cue-10",
      "transcript": "He had not sold a Vermeer. He had sold the belief that it was one.",
      "file": "audio/vermeer-forgery/narration/cue-10.wav",
      "start": 78.63333333333334,
      "duration": 4.125,
      "beatIndex": 9,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "vermeer-forgery.asset.forgery-defense.script.10",
      "samples": 99000,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    }
  ],
